      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A school opened in Liberty in 1838, one of the earliest educational institutions in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/liberty-tx-liberty-county",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Around 1910, Liberty housed three cotton gins, a gristmill, and a cigar factory, showing its early industrial mix.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/liberty-tx-liberty-county",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Texas and New Orleans Railroad reached Liberty in 1858, turning it into a shipping hub and prompting construction of a Market House by 1860.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/liberty-tx-liberty-county",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Liberty’s Sam Houston Regional Library and Research Center, opened in 1977, holds the world’s largest collection of Sam Houston photographs and illustrations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
